UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'partial', verified_at = NULL,
  evidence = evidence || ' | W2-F-C 2026-11-05: PARTIAL, read live. SECRETS-STORE-BIND-1 is built and live: qnfo-ops 2.65.0 (PR 7659, merged 03:53:06Z, deployed 03:53:40Z, /health read 04:25:53Z) parses [[secrets_store_secrets]] in installDeclaredBindings and installs the binding only for a name in ops_config secrets_store_bind_allow (created empty by migrations/2026-11-05-w2f-c-secrets-store-allow.sql, read empty) that the Secrets Store lists with the workers scope, with a 135-check offline suite; an unreadable allowlist or store, a missing entry or a refused deploy skips the binding and never fails the deploy. The qnfo-infra deploy of 04:26:14Z (1.14.0-lake-spine, bindings_preserved 13) wrote the ledger note "secrets_store_secrets: 1 declared, 0 bound, skipped CF_TOKEN_STORE:not in secrets_store_bind_allow": the installer ran on the real worker and bound nothing, as designed (the CF_API_TOKEN store entry dates from 2026-07-04 and infraSecret prefers the store with no fallback). agent_issues 1001969 and 1001981 closed on their code-probes. Still open: SECRETS-STORE-ADOPT-1 (agent_issues 1001970). Found while reading the consumers: qnfo-ai (6 lines of worker.js) and qnfo-tools-mcp (1) use env.INFRA_TOKEN as a string, so a store binding (an object with get()) needs a helper that takes either, and a binding name different from the legacy secret, before the allowlist and the one-PATCH rotation drill; scripts/cf_ops_actions.py (action secrets-store-adopt) follows. Provider keys stay with the owner.'
WHERE id = 51 AND instr(evidence, ' | W2-F-C 2026-11-05') = 0;

