UPDATE agent_issues
SET description = description || char(10) || 'W2-F-C 2026-11-05: SECRETS-STORE-BIND-1 is live (qnfo-ops 2.65.0, ops_config secrets_store_bind_allow empty, qnfo-infra deploy of 04:26:14Z bound nothing and noted it). Read while preparing this step: qnfo-ai (worker.js lines 2979-2984, 4992-4996, 5010-5014) and qnfo-tools-mcp (line 342) send env.INFRA_TOKEN as a string in an Authorization header, and qnfo-infra checks it through infraSecret(env, "INFRA_TOKEN"). A secrets_store_secret binding gives env.X an object with get(), so the order is: (1) one change per consumer that resolves a value that is either a string or a binding (the pattern of infraSecret), with a test; (2) wrangler.toml [[secrets_store_secrets]] with a binding name that differs from the legacy secret (for example INFRA_TOKEN_STORE) on the four consumers; (3) the store entry INFRA_TOKEN written with the same value as the legacy secret under the secret lock (the action secrets-store-adopt in scripts/cf_ops_actions.py, which prints no value); (4) the allowlist entry in ops_config secrets_store_bind_allow; (5) the one-PATCH rotation drill with the old value refused and the new one accepted. Step 1 needs no secret and can start now.'
WHERE id = 1001970 AND status = 'open' AND instr(description, char(10) || 'W2-F-C 2026-11-05') = 0;
